## Factorial of a positive integer (both ways)

------------------------------------------
#include <stdio.h>

long long factRec(int n) {               /* recursion */
    if (n <= 1) return 1;
    return n * factRec(n - 1);
}

long long factLoop(int n) {              /* iteration */
    long long f = 1;
    for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++)
        f = f * i;
    return f;
}

int main(void) {
    printf("Recursive: 10! = %lld\n", factRec(10));
    printf("Iterative: 10! = %lld\n", factLoop(10));
    return 0;
}
------------------------------------------

## Output

------------------------------------------
Recursive: 10! = 3628800
Iterative: 10! = 3628800
------------------------------------------

• Either version earns the marks; the question does not demand recursion.
• n! = 1 × 2 × … × n, and 0! = 1. Use long long: 13! already overflows a 32-bit int.

Exam tip: read n with scanf("%d", &n); and reject n < 0 before calling.

